# rule.forbid.gerunds

no gerunds (-ing words used as nouns) in names, comments, docs, logs, commits. they blur noun vs verb, hide agency, and signal a lazy placeholder for an unclear domain term
replace with a verb, an agent, a result, or an explicit state:
| 👎 | 👍 |
|---|---|
| existing | found, current, prior |
| processing | process, processor, processed |
| handling | handle, handler |
| loading | load, loader, loaded |
| running | run, runner, active |
| pending | queued, awaited |
| missing | absent, lacks |
| remaining | left, rest |
| matching | matched, match, fits |
no exceptions. prefer explicit state (`status === 'active'`)
enforcement: gerund usage = blocker (a hook also blocks writes that contain them)
